# X6.2b: response headers for the static front at the final edge (Cloudflare static assets / Pages read this file from
# the build output; Vite copies public/ there unchanged). The page also sets the same policy itself (index.html
# <meta name="referrer">), so it holds on a host that ignores this file.
#
# Referrer-Policy is strict-origin-when-cross-origin, deliberately NOT no-referrer: under no-referrer a browser sends
# `Origin: null` on every non-CORS POST (Fetch "append a request Origin header"), including the cross-origin step-up
# re-authentication form POST (features/auth/stepup/StepUpHost.tsx -> POST /auth/<provider>/reauthenticate), whose
# server-side Origin check refuses `null`. strict-origin-when-cross-origin keeps the real Origin, and a cross-origin
# Referer carries the origin only, never a path or query string (XA-08: the forgot-password address in the URL never
# reaches a third party such as the font host).
#
# Nothing in this repository deploys this file to an edge today; the <meta name="referrer"> in index.html is the
# effective control. This file applies once the front is served by Cloudflare static assets / Pages.
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
